/**
 * Material Symbols Rounded artwork for the icons that have an unambiguous
 * equivalent, keyed by the name this component already answered to.
 *
 * WHY A PATH AND NOT `<MaterialSymbol>`. The obvious migration is to delegate
 * to {@link ./MaterialSymbol.tsx}, which is what the 94 Remixicon call sites
 * did. It cannot be done here, and the reason is not a matter of taste: that
 * component renders a `<span>`, and 143 CSS rules across 31 stylesheets select
 * this component's output as an *element* — `.chrome-action > svg:first-child`,
 * `.mention-item > svg`, `.od-select-trigger[aria-expanded='true'] svg`,
 * `.subtab-pill button:has(> svg:only-child)` and so on. Those rules carry
 * sizes, tonal backgrounds, colours, `display: block` and the 180-degree
 * rotation that flips a select's chevron. Swapping the element to a `<span>`
 * detaches every one of them at once, in a way no test in this repository
 * asserts and no type error reports — the icons would still render, in the
 * wrong size, the wrong colour, and without the rotation. Keeping the `<svg>`
 * keeps all 143 selectors matching, so the migration changes the artwork and
 * nothing else.
 *
 * PROVENANCE. Every `d` below was extracted from the bundled variable font at
 * `public/fonts/material-symbols/material-symbols-rounded.woff2` — the same
 * bytes `MaterialSymbol` renders — instantiated at `opsz` 24 and at the stated
 * `FILL`, with the y axis negated for SVG's downward y. Hence the 960-unit
 * `viewBox` these render into, which is Material Symbols' own icon box. The
 * outlines are therefore identical to what the font would draw; they were not
 * traced, redrawn or generated. `symbol` records which glyph each one is so the
 * mapping stays auditable, and every name was checked against the 3,967
 * ligature targets the font actually carries rather than against a remembered
 * name — see `smartphone`, which is not one of them.
 *
 * WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. Fourteen names keep their original inline
 * artwork below, and the switch is still the fallback for them:
 *
 *   `discord`, `github`, `github-filled` — brand marks. Material Symbols
 *     carries no brand logo at all, and substituting one is a trademark
 *     question rather than an icon one. This is the same exception
 *     `SocialShareGrid.tsx` already relies on.
 *   `blocks`, `fork`, `hammer`, `integrations-filled`, `layout`, `panel-left`,
 *     `present`, `slides`, `sliders`, `sun-moon`, `swatchbook` — no equivalent
 *     that is clearly right. Each has a *plausible* candidate (`widgets`,
 *     `account_tree`, `hardware`, `hub`, `view_quilt`, `dock_to_right`,
 *     `monitor`, `slideshow`, `tune`, `routine`, `style`), and a plausible
 *     wrong icon is the failure mode worth avoiding: it renders, it looks
 *     deliberate, and nothing catches it. They stay until someone can compare
 *     them on screen.
 */
